  "query_preview": "/Saturday through Wednesday/...\nIssued 334 AM MDT WED AUG 26 2026\nUpper level trough over BC will continue over the long term with\nbelow normal temperatures and a slight chance of showers and\nthunderstorms. Temperatures will be near normal Saturday \nbefore cooling to below normal Sunday as a dry cold front moves\nthrough. Another trough digging along the BC coast will shift\nthe flow to southwest on Monday, and bring warmer temperatures\nahead of the next cold front. A cold front will move through the\narea on Tuesday bringing cooler temperatures and below normal\ntemperatures Tuesday and Wednesday. Uncertainty remains elevated\nin the extended period, as tropical activity in the Pacific \nenhances the jet stream. Models do not handle the energy \ntransfer well in these situations so expect lots of changes in \nthe far extended period over the next week.",
